    "title": "ITU ARIS Lab. Acoustic Drone Dataset",
    "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22682339",
    "publication_date": "2026-09-10",
    "description": "<p><strong>An acoustic dataset for drone detection.</strong></p>\n<p>The recordings were made outdoors in a single continuous session, with several drone models flown through a range of manoeuvres at distances from a few metres out to roughly two kilometres. Weather, wind and background traffic were whatever the day provided; nothing was staged.</p>\n<p>The audio is split into one-second segments and labelled in two classes, drone and background. Ready-made train/validation/test splits are included, along with a file mapping each segment back to the part of the session it came from. Use that mapping rather than splitting the files at random &mdash; neighbouring segments overlap, so a random split puts the same audio on both sides. The included README explains the layout and the known limitations of the set.</p>\n<p><strong>Collected and released by the ARIS Laboratory, Department of Electronics and Communication Engineering, Istanbul Technical University.</strong></p>",
